{
    "background_story": "Everly was a vibrant and charismatic Colombian dancer who brought the rhythms of her homeland to the world stage. Born in the vibrant city of Cartagena, she grew up surrounded by the sounds of salsa, vallenato, and cumbia. Everly's passion for dance was ignited by her abuela, who taught her the traditional steps and movements of Colombian folklore. As she honed her craft, Everly became a sought-after performer, traveling the globe to share the energy and beauty of Colombian dance. Her troupe, 'Ritmos del Sol', was a testament to the country's rich cultural heritage, and Everly's infectious enthusiasm won the hearts of audiences everywhere. Through her art, she remained deeply connected to her Colombian roots, inspiring others to experience the warmth and joy of her beloved culture.",
